who lives who dies who returns to the  afterlife from whence they came and most  importantly who gets slimed this is the  ending of ghostbusters afterlife  explained obviously spoilers ahead  arguably the most important character in  ghostbusters afterlife is phoebe the  brilliant young granddaughter of egon  spengler it's phoebe who cracks open the  mystery at the heart of the film and  forms a connection across generations of  her estranged family in the process at  the beginning of the film phoebe is an  outsider not just in somerville but in  her own family by the end of the film  she's the heart of her extended new  family and friend group a hero to the  world and a newly minted ghostbuster  continuing the tradition set up by her  late grandfather we see bibi's journey  to self-actualization but the question  remains what happens to her next it's  easy to imagine her as the first junior  member of the ghostbusters attending a  fancy science-based new york city school  by day and wielding a proton pack by  night it's also easy to see her staying  in summerville for a while archiving and  continuing her grandfather's work as she  digs deeper into the mysteries of gozer  whatever happens phoebe has a bright  future not just because of what she's  achieved but because she's learned how  to really be herself  though his personal journey in the film  is considerably less developed than his  sisters trevor spengler still gets an  arc across ghostbusters afterlife though  he definitely considers himself the cool  one in his family trevor is still a bit  of an outsider thanks to his fresh  arrival in somerville by the end of the  film trevor has become a ghostbuster of  sorts alongside his sister despite his  lack of scientific knowledge or  particular enthusiasm for the paranormal  what he does have though is a sizable  sense of mechanical wisdom as evidenced  by his ability to fix ecto-1 with only a  tiny bit of supernatural help from his  grandfather it's easy to see him  sticking around somerville but it's just  as easy to see him moving to new york  city where trevor could become the  winston of the next generation of  ghostbusters  he's not a scientist but he's a hard  worker with a sharp mind and he's  willing to dig in deep for the people he  cares about  at the beginning of the film callie  spengler feels like a failed mother she  hasn't been able to make life in the  city work out her kids are growing and  changing in ways she doesn't fully  understand and her only refuge in life  is a broken down old house in the middle  of oklahoma left to her by a father who  never had time for  but like every other member of her  family over the course of the story cali  finds a new sense of purpose and  realizes the father she never really  knew not only cared about her but did  everything he could to protect her from  forces she couldn't understand at the  time a new sense of purpose also comes  through the arrival of gary gruberson  the local seismologist and teacher who  not only adores her but adores her kids  as well so what happens to them next  having made peace with their families  past callie seems ready to build a new  future with gary whether that's in  somerville new york city or somewhere  else entirely a new family unit has  grown out of the ashes of the old one  though much of the film centers on the  spengler family a good portion of the  plots and ghostbusters afterlife is  pushed forward by the kid known as  podcast phoebe's summer school friend  with a deep interest in mysteries and  other assorted occult lore though phoebe  brings the scientific know-how and  observational powers to the team podcast  brings the belief in the supernatural  that allows her to see what's right in  front of her and the research skills to  dig into what's really going on by the  end of the film it's clear that he's  basically the raymond stance of the new  ghostbusters team and rey himself makes  it clear that he's a fan of the young  podcaster obviously podcast's role in  what went down in oklahoma could mean a  big boost to his subscriber base  provided enough people know that  anything went down at all but it will  also mean his appetite for more  supernatural mysteries will only grow  with time  ghostbusters afterlife is largely set in  somerville oklahoma an out of the way  former mining town that's basically a  tiny dot on the map with seemingly  nothing to show for itself by the end of  the film though somerville has become  the epicenter of supernatural activity  on earth as the discovery of a temple  built by an eccentric architect to  summon an ancient sumerian god propels  the ghostbusters into a new adventure  after gozer was trapped by the team  things seemed poised to quiet down at  somerville and we see the old ecto-1 car  back in action in new york city but that  doesn't mean the oklahoma town won't get  any more attention if it truly did serve  as the force behind a supernatural  re-awakening it's bound to attract all  manner of investigators scientists  tourists and media podcasts won't be the  only person investigating its mysteries  anymore and that could both lead to good  and bad things from the town alleged  ghost sightings and related supernatural  occurrences have been reported across  the entire tri-state area in the  original ghostbusters the team faced  gozer as the ancient god took the form  of a giant representation of the stay  pup marshmallow man after crossing the  streams of their proton packs the  ghostbusters were able to defeat gozer's  destroyer form and thus banish the god  back to its own dimension seemingly for  good of course we now know that gozer  was just biting their time until they  could re-enter our dimension but  thankfully egon spangler had developed a  plan instead of just banishing the  creature yet again he built an elaborate  high-powered trap on his homestead in  oklahoma waiting for the moment that he  could lure gozer in and spring it it  didn't work for egon but his  granddaughter her family and friends and  the surviving original ghostbusters were  able to capture the creature the  question is if gozer now contained in a  trap what happens next there's a good  chance gozer will need to be busted at  least one more time  over the course of the film the mystery  at the heart of ghostbusters afterlife  is slowly unearthed often quite  literally eventually phoebe trevor  podcast and lucky discover a tombslash  temple complex beneath the mountain  built in tribute to gozer a sumerian god  who first appeared in the original  ghostbusters film the tomb is full of  interesting details but phoebe picks up  one in particular that stands out with  regard to the franchise's future a stone  relief that features carved dates of  various years in which major  catastrophes occurred what's especially  interesting about these carvings is that  there appears to be another partially  obscured date carved into the rock  sometime after 2021 it's difficult to  make out exactly when it is but gozer's  closest followers probably have some  idea and the presence of the temple in  oklahoma suggests there could be others  out there so what future catastrophe  awaits this next generation of  ghostbusters time will tell  ghostbusters afterlife is a movie packed  with cameo appearances though she was  confirmed to be a part of the film  months before its release one former  ghostbusters star waited until the very  end to show up dana barrett who  developed a romance with dr peter  venkman in the first film and rekindled  it in a second dana finally appears in a  mid-credits scene in the film that  echoes our first meeting with bankman  back in 1984 as she runs his old shock  treatment esp test on him there's clear  flirtation happening between the two of  them and bankman even throws out the  phrase true love at one point it's such  a brief scene that we don't get too many  clues but it's clear that the filmmakers  at least want us to think about what  might be happening perhaps an eventual  afterlife sequel could clear up just how  well peter and dana are getting along  these days  in one crucial scene in ghostbusters  afterlife bibi calls the old number in a  vintage ghostbusters commercial and is  connected to ray stance's a cult book  shop in new york city after a little  nudging she's able to get ready to tell  her a little of the backstory behind the  breakup of the ghostbusters according to  rey it had its roots in two things  egon's obsession with the re-emergence  of gozer and an almost complete lack of  new calls for supernatural assistance  there hasn't been a ghost sighting in 30  years gozer's return obviously shook at  least a few ghosts loose and at the very  end of the film we see ecto-1 back in  action but how many ghosts are there to  really bust gozer is after all in  captivity now and the portal that  awakened the god of destruction seems to  be dormant has something else shaken  loose that will guarantee continued work  for the team or are they just going to  do what they can with what they have for  as long as possible obviously a sequel  would help to clear this up quite a bit  in the post-credits scene of  ghostbusters afterlife winston zettamore  and janine melnitz meet new york city to  discuss the future of the ghostbusters  team winston's success in the world of  finance means that he has considerable  resources at his disposal enough to buy  back the firehouse restore ecto-1 and  get the team up and running again the  question remaining is what exactly that  team will look like once winston and  janine are all set up again will the  spangler family move back to new york  and be part of the next era of the  company with janine and winston running  the show behind the scenes it seems  likely that if winston and janine are  back in the game rey would have a hard  time not lurking around the firehouse  himself training new recruits and  venkman well he might not care for  busting anymore but even if he doesn't  he could be persuaded to handle the  marketing side of things it's easy to  imagine the crew coming together with  the spanglers to launch the next phase  of ghostbusters incorporated and perhaps  even do what previous sequel ideas had  in mind and franchise the whole thing  when locations in every major city  whatever the case the old firehouse is  about to power up again and that trap  grid in the basement might have a few  old terrors still lurking in it  though phoebe is the star of  ghostbusters afterlife you could make  the case that the most important  character in the overall story is  actually her deceased grandfather dr  egon spangler by the time of afterlife  egon is a ghost lurking in his house in  oklahoma and biding his time until his  genius granddaughter puts all the pieces  of his plant to defeat gozer together  while that happens we learned that  somewhere along the way he decided he  had to make a massive sacrifice in his  quest to keep the world safe from a dark  god when he couldn't convince his fellow  ghostbusters that gozer was about to  resurge egon instead cut himself off  from everyone with the exception of  janine moved to oklahoma to be near the  old gozer sites and abandoned both his  family and his friends for their own  protection do you have any hobbies  i collect spores molds and fungus  it's a move that speaks to his obsessive  nature but also to his ability to think  in terms of the greater good egon's  choices could easily be dismissed as  part of his character as the coldest  ghostbuster but it took an enormous  level of love and care for the people in  his life to do what he did it was a  sacrifice that the film only scratched  the surface of but in the end it proved  that egon spangler may have had the  biggest heart of all of the ghostbusters  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

